//! time/instant — monotonic clock reading.
//!
//! Status: runnable (Phase 6/Wave 0, ADR-020). Monotonic
//! milliseconds since a process-wide arbitrary epoch: the contract
//! is the DURATION BETWEEN READS, never a wall-clock date. This is
//! the one time primitive Phase 6 needs for rate limiting,
//! deadlines, sliding windows, and OTel timestamps.
//!
//! No timezone, calendar, or date interpretation here — those need
//! a tz database and are explicitly a non-goal (ADR-020).
//! Milliseconds since a process-wide arbitrary epoch (monotonic:
//! never decreases within a process). Values are non-negative and
//! fit `Int` comfortably; only differences between two readings are
//! meaningful.
//!
//! Plain `fn` (no `export`): stdlib is distributed by the pre-import
//! concat model (stdlib/SPEC.md §1), where the whole file is a root
//! and `export` markers are not part of the surface — same as
//! `net/http/*` and `db/*`.

fn instant_now_ms() -> Int:
    time_mono_ms_builtin()
